{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_62","type":"agent_message","text":"The behavioral mismatches are test-harness interference, not C/Rust output: libtest runs tests in parallel and writes progress text while file descriptors are temporarily redirected. I’m converting the row functions into one sequential completion-gate test so only ABI output can enter the capture. Separately, debug Rust turns a null dereference into `SIGABRT`; I’m matching C’s observed `SIGSEGV` explicitly for null `argv`, while null elements still flow into libc exactly as C does."}}
